Package: my-xymon-extensions-server
Version: @VERSION@-1
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: xymon
Suggests: my-xymon-extensions
Maintainer: roemer2201 <r.oliver@web.de>
Homepage: https://github.com/roemer2201/my-xymon-extensions
Description: Xymon server configuration for my-xymon-extensions
 Server-side configuration for the extensions in the
 my-xymon-extensions package: the settings that turn their status and
 data messages into RRD files and trend graphs.
 .
 This package belongs on the Xymon SERVER, the client package belongs
 on the monitored hosts. The two are independent - a server collecting
 data from clients elsewhere needs only this one.
 .
 Everything is installed as drop-in files, so no stock Xymon
 configuration file is modified:
  * /etc/xymon/xymonserver.d/ - TEST2RRD, NCV_*/SPLITNCV_* and GRAPHS
    settings per extension (read via graphs-include.cfg/
    xymonserver-include.cfg, which Debian's init script regenerates
    at every start).
  * /etc/xymon/graphs.d/ - the graph definitions.
  * /etc/xymon/rrddefinitions.d/ - RRA archive layout; needed by the
    if_link extension so that single link changes stay visible in
    long-range graphs. Debian does not ship this drop-in directory,
    so one "optional directory" line has to be added to
    rrddefinitions.cfg once - the post-install output says so if it
    is missing.
 .
 Covered extensions: smart, temp, la, memory, opkg, fritzdsl,
 fritzwan, wifi, if_link, lxc and xymonext. The disk extension needs no
 server-side configuration - it reports into the standard disk column,
 which the server parses itself.
